# Variable-grid train

Retrospective source review · fit-3955a792ed6c415a

Authored interpretation of captured source and receipts. No new training, benchmark, lineage or scientific promotion is implied.

**Method.** An additive pressure-correction CNN with 371,729 float32 parameters in 38 tensors. Four encoder widths 8/16/24/32, bottleneck 48 and decoder widths 32/24/16/8; two 3x3x3 convolutions per block, affine-free four-group GroupNorm and SiLU, a bottleneck global-mean broadcast and nearest-to-skip upsampling. The network consumes seven inputs: residual, previous pressure, physical XYZ coordinates, rho and dt; spacing also affects the coordinates and remains scalar FV metadata. Its linear 1x1x1 head is scaled to physical pressure, gauged by the first correction cell and added to the previous pressure. FV arithmetic and the pressure output remain float64. All network parameters are optimized. The captured input budget is 65,536 cells. This operation proposes pressure for one request; it does not advance the physical simulation.

**Purpose.** Qualify CUDA training and typed restoration of the seven-channel CNN through a deliberately short 20-update fit.

**Experiment.** 20 Adam updates at learning rate 0.001, batch size 2 and seed 20261015, with gradient clipping. Four training trajectories supply 96 pressure frames; two validation trajectories supply 48 frames. The shared 9,296,002-byte dataset covers 8 and 16 cells per metre. Training grids are 8x8x8, 9x7x5, 16x16x16 and 17x13x9; validation grids are 12x8x6 and 24x16x12. The recorded forcing labels are steady and moving, with amplitude 0.5 m/s2 and a 1/60 s timestep. The objective equally weights normalized squared pressure-field and FV equation-residual errors. Train-only scales and the exact PCG64 draw sequence are bound. The recipe supplies a final-update candidate and does not retain an optimizer-resume state.

**Observed outcome.** The original final logged training loss is 0.37520032356475808 at update 20. The existing 128-request GPU comparison gives worst mean-free pressure relative L2 0.29082935903787244 and equation relative L2 0.47509410708509614. The training objective and common field errors are different quantities. This source review adds no inference timing or own-history drift measurement.

**Lesson.** This is CUDA enablement with a short fitting budget. It shares C04 initial tensors, dataset and the first 20 optimizer sample draws. The original recipe verifies CUDA gradients and Adam moments, then transfers the final model to CPU for deployment/parity inference. Its recorded maximum CPU/CUDA pressure difference is 9.715233779570773e-09 on that historical population. Different final update budgets prevent a matched-budget training comparison.

**Reproduction.** Use the captured project manifest and training recipe, exact source witness, config, runtime, normalization and two typed data slots. Preserve the initial seed inventory and final weight hash. The population metadata retains native binary identity 67d03c454e8293fd0120243c5834e8f67e4a24f2ba66392fef9a815d7b9117ad. Its six capture specifications and frame hashes describe the original data. Clean training/data regeneration and conversion to the new Rheon have not been executed or qualified. The original CUDA recipe ends with CPU deployment/parity inference. Do not execute it unchanged under the current no-CPU-neural-forward policy; a clean GPU-only reproducer remains to be qualified.

